          <article class="archive-item" id="post-20282">
            <p class="archive-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-13">13 October 2026</time> &middot; on The Hacker News</p>
            <h3>Product Walkthrough: Bitdefender AI Visibility and Control</h3>
            <p>Bitdefender&#x27;s AI Visibility and Control helps administrators identify and manage AI tools in their environment by categorizing them and assessing risk without inspecting credentials.</p>
            <p>A traditional software inventory misses the AI tools running in your environment. Browser-based assistants, editor extensions, local model runtimes, and MCP servers slip through the cracks. They don’t show up in installed programs or network traffic logs. This leaves administrators guessing about what’s running and how risky it is.</p>
            <p>Bitdefender’s AI Visibility and Control fills this gap. It identifies AI services, their configuration, and risk scores without inspecting prompts or credentials. It categorizes tools into 17 functional groups, making it easier to align with your policies. A high risk score doesn’t mean removal—it’s a signal to act.</p>
            <p>The tool provides two views: AI Findings highlights the most urgent risks, while AI Services gives a full picture of each tool. These views help you prioritize and understand the scope of exposure. A zero risk score doesn’t mean approval—it just means the tool isn’t misconfigured.</p>
            <p>This approach lets you enforce policies where they already live: web filtering, custom rules, and PHASR. You get visibility without overstepping, and control without disruption. It’s a practical step toward managing AI risk in your environment.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="archive-item" id="post-20264">
            <p class="archive-meta"><time datetime="2026-10-13">13 October 2026</time> &middot; on The Hacker News</p>
            <h3>[Webinar] How to Stop AI-Driven Privilege Escalation With Runtime Identity Controls</h3>
            <p>Runtime identity controls are crucial for mitigating AI-driven privilege escalation by enabling real-time access evaluation and response.</p>
            <p>Runtime identity controls are becoming essential in the fight against AI-driven privilege escalation. The danger of a stolen identity isn&#x27;t just in the initial access but in what follows. AI can exploit vulnerabilities and escalate privileges faster than traditional systems can respond. This creates a critical gap in how we manage access and behavior.</p>
            <p>Traditional identity security focuses on authentication and permissions but fails when a trusted identity is compromised or its behavior changes. AI-powered attacks can automate the attack chain while defenders are still investigating. The answer lies in real-time evaluation and control of access during active use. This is where runtime identity security shines.</p>
            <p>Runtime identity security evaluates access continuously and enforces security decisions as threats evolve. It allows defenders to adapt to AI-driven attacks that move at machine speed. Security teams must know not just who has access but whether that access should still be trusted right now. This approach closes the gap between detection and response.</p>
            <p>The next identity attack may not give you time to react. Building a strategy that keeps pace with modern threats requires more than traditional controls. It demands runtime identity security as a core component of your defense. Stay ahead of the curve.</p>
          </article>
