            <p>The unified policy fabric from Elisity ensures least-privilege access for all identities, including AI agents. By combining identity context with quantum security, organizations can prioritize post-quantum upgrades based on business risk and operational importance. This approach bridges the gap between current security investments and future quantum readiness without disrupting essential operations.</p>
            <p>Preparing for the quantum era requires coordinated changes across applications and infrastructure. Elisity’s platform enables enterprises to protect critical connections and restrict unnecessary access during the transition. This is especially vital in sectors like healthcare and critical infrastructure, where legacy systems will coexist with post-quantum cryptography for years.</p>
            <p>The partnership underscores the importance of governance, audit, and control in managing AI agents and quantum risks. As we move toward self-healing zero trust policies, the focus remains on preserving existing deployments while modernizing at a sustainable pace. This collaboration sets a governance framework for agentic AI in a post-quantum world.</p>
