            <h3>Social Engineering AI Agents: The New BEC for 2026</h3>
            <p>AI agents are now targets for social engineering attacks that can manipulate them into unauthorized actions by exploiting prompt injection and malicious content.</p>
            <p>AI agents are becoming new targets for social engineering, much like how BEC attacks target employees. Attackers can manipulate these agents into taking authorized actions by exploiting prompt injection and feeding malicious content. This shifts the focus from training humans to also securing non-human identities.</p>
            <p>The risk is real. Attackers can steal data, redirect payments, or gain a foothold in systems by tricking agents into acting on false instructions. Unlike humans, AI agents don’t experience emotions, so attacks rely on how they interpret commands and establish trust. This means we must rethink how we secure and govern these systems.</p>
